Subject: Tolerate unwritable/closed log fd during libpas and Fil-C panic logging
Policy-Class: P1-Toolchain
Rationale: When a program triggers a Fil-C memory safety panic after closing fd 2 (for example PHP 7.0 CLI closing STDERR during request shutdown before hitting a Phar stream UAF) or when stderr is a broken pipe, write_panic_context() returns false and filc_finish_panicking() trips PAS_ASSERT(write_panic_context(log_fd, context)), while pas_fd_stream_vprintf() trips PAS_ASSERT(errno == EINTR) on EBADF/EPIPE. That causes a recursive panic in pas_panic() and terminates with __builtin_trap() (SIGILL) instead of completing the safety panic cleanly (SIGTRAP via pas_crash_with_info_impl or exit 42 under FILC_EXIT_ON_PANIC). Give up writing on non-EINTR write errors or zero-byte writes in pas_fd_stream_vprintf(), and ignore write_panic_context() failure in filc_finish_panicking().
Upstream-Status: Upstream-Candidate (pizlonator/fil-c)
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: none
Origin-Kind: local-fix

diff --git a/libpas/src/libpas/pas_fd_stream.c b/libpas/src/libpas/pas_fd_stream.c
index 1111111111..2222222222 100644
--- a/libpas/src/libpas/pas_fd_stream.c
+++ b/libpas/src/libpas/pas_fd_stream.c
@@ -79,11 +79,13 @@ void pas_fd_stream_vprintf(pas_fd_stream* stream, const char* format, va_list ar
         result = write(stream->fd, ptr, bytes_left_to_write);
 #endif
         if (result < 0) {
-            PAS_ASSERT(errno == EINTR);
-            continue;
+            if (errno == EINTR)
+                continue;
+            return;
         }
 
-        PAS_ASSERT(result);
+        if (!result)
+            return;
 
         ptr += result;
         bytes_left_to_write -= (size_t)result;
diff --git a/libpas/src/libpas/filc_runtime.c b/libpas/src/libpas/filc_runtime.c
index 3333333333..4444444444 100644
--- a/libpas/src/libpas/filc_runtime.c
+++ b/libpas/src/libpas/filc_runtime.c
@@ -4484,7 +4484,7 @@ PAS_NO_RETURN void filc_finish_panicking(filc_panic_context* context, const char
     
     if (filc_exit_on_panic) {
         if (!filc_quiet_panic) {
-            PAS_ASSERT(write_panic_context(log_fd, context));
+            (void)write_panic_context(log_fd, context);
             pas_log("[%d] filc panic: %s\n", pas_getpid(), kind_string);
         }
         _exit(42);
@@ -4526,6 +4526,6 @@ PAS_NO_RETURN void filc_finish_panicking(filc_panic_context* context, const char
         }
     }
 
-    PAS_ASSERT(write_panic_context(log_fd, context));
+    (void)write_panic_context(log_fd, context);
     pas_panic("%s\n", kind_string);
 }
